Nested Subqueries
A common use of subqueries is to perform tests for ‘set membership’, ‘make set comparisons’, and ‘determine set cardinality’ by nesting subqueries in the WHERE clause.
IN connective tests for set membership, where the set is a collection of values produced by a SELECT clause. 
NOT IN connective tests for the absence of set membership.

